<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3696] .NET: Java type mapping does not work with nullable types</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3696</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;See JavaTypes class. We should probably map nullables there too.&lt;br/&gt;
Java has everything nullable by default, need to explain to the users that anything can be null underneath.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Make sure to test this with &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;QuerySqlField&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Workaround is to use manual QueryEntity configuration and specify either non-nullable .NET type, or the Java type name.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
